### 3. Termux Environment Escalation (`airoot` / `su -c`)
* **Bridging the Terminal**: To cross the app boundary, the terminal session invokes the root wrapper alias (`airoot`, which maps to `su -c`).
* **UID Transition**: This shifts the effective process execution context from standard user ID (`u0_aXXX`) directly to **UID 0 (Root)**. This grants unhindered read/write capabilities across all raw block devices, procfs entries, sysfs trees, and system-level directories (`/data/adb/`, `/system/`, `/proc/`, `/sys/`).

